{
  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "timer-effect-steer-late-budget",
    "parent": "timer-effect-steer",
    "kind": "add",
    "title": "Apply inert-timer damping only after a run passes a budget fraction",
    "description": "Same Beta(fired, acted) per (node, resume vertex, in-flight) key as timer-effect-steer, but the multiplier in score_runnable is identity until steps_used/step_budget exceeds a threshold read from config (timer_effect_steer.late_fraction, default off/1.0), after which it damps provably-inert idle firings. Early exploration keeps the unmodified admission order that the h1/h2/h3 corpora depend on; only the tail of a run that is heading for iteration exhaustion is steered. Reuses timer_steer counters plus a new timer_steer.gated_early counter. Gate behind the existing timer_effect_steer field so default behavior is unchanged.",
    "category": "scheduler",
    "buildsOn": [
      "timer_effect",
      "score_runnable",
      "termination step accounting"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 6,
    "expectedCost": 2,
    "rationale": "The parent showed the depth gain is real and large in the tail (d>=8 +28%) while the h2/h1/h3 loss tracks throughput rather than per-run coverage; restricting the multiplier to the 73% of runs that exhaust their budget should retain the depth tail while cutting both the per-candidate scoring cost and the early-order perturbation that the sequential h2 gate punished.",
    "generalityArgument": "Keys only on budget fraction consumed, CFG resume vertex, and whether a delivery is in flight — all protocol-independent runtime state; a protocol whose timers act is never damped regardless of phase.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-29T15:40:00Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "[operator-requeued] The restored epoch-8 implementation no longer compiles: post-boxing-allocation-resweep put WaitingReader behind Arc<(Record, Lhs)> and the timer code assigns the bare tuple. A text merge was clean; the type check was not. Re-implement against current HEAD. Prior evidence: 8 chunks, 2,058,060 runs, depth>=7 pGreater 0.977, per-run d7 +4.3% and d8 +11.2% at flat throughput; the mechanism fired 3,014,627 times and idle timer firings act at 6.0% against 16.8% with a delivery in flight."
  },
